# 0. API-wide rules: documentation, versioned paths, unified error format, security headers.
#
# VS Code "REST Client" extension: click "Send Request" above each request.
# No login needed in this file.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@api = {{baseUrl}}/api/v1


### OpenAPI document → 200 (Swagger UI: http://localhost:8080/swagger)
# Every path starts with /api/v1, and the "Bearer" security scheme gives Swagger its Authorize button.
GET {{baseUrl}}/openapi/v1.json

### Unified error format + security headers → 401
# Body: Problem Details (application/problem+json) with type, title, status, instance, traceId.
# Headers: X-Content-Type-Options, X-Frame-Options, Referrer-Policy, Content-Security-Policy, and no "Server" header.
GET {{api}}/auth/me

### Same error format for a missing resource → 404, with "detail"
GET {{api}}/products/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001

### Same error format for invalid input → 422, with "errors" per field
GET {{api}}/products?pageSize=1000
